Brent J. Nordquist wrote:
>
> 1. Are there any monsters that will loot my stash if I don't lock it? Any
> advantage to using a chest vs. a large box?

None will.  The only difference is weight.

> 2. Prayer timeout: I've seen lots of references that there is one, but
> how do you calculate the actual value?

The actual value is determined when you pray and it is random
within a range.  So the various ranges can be listed but the value
you get at any one time can't be listed.

> 4. Rusted/burnt and corroded/rotted: Are these "erosion" damages somehow
> paired the way I've listed them here? I know about reading enchant
> armor/weapon while confused, and that !oOil restores rusted and corroded
> items... any other way to restore burnt and rotted items?

If you wield a damaged weapon and pray there is a chance that
damage will be repaired.  Your diety must no be angry, your
prayer timeout must be down to zero, your luck must be positive
and the exact value of your luck effects the chances of this
happening.  Basically if your weapons started your prayer
uncursed and ended up blessed, any damage would have been
repaired as well.

> 5. I've seen references to naming one's weapons Sting or Orcrist; what
> does that do? (I use daggers.)

Named weapons have specific advantages.  Some advantages
apply across the board, others only against specific types of
monsters.  Those two names only effect the several types of
"o"rc monsters (including orcish mummy and orcish zombie).

Note that some artifacts have alignments.  When your diety
gives you a gift weapon it is either of your alignment or unaligned.
Those two are chaotic so only chaotics can get them as gifts.
Those two chaotic artifacts are available to any character by
means other than a gift.  There are two lawfull artifacts that can
be gotten by any character later in the game and one neutral
artifact that is remotely possible in the late game but those
occur in the hands of monsters.

